    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (68.91) and **Will Smith** (67.40) anchor the lineup as our most reliable offensive threats. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** maintains elite status despite a neutral platoon matchup against Leiter, as his prime #2 spot in the order guarantees high-leverage opportunities. **Will Smith** benefits from the most favorable matchup of the day, facing Jack Kochanowicz\u2019s bloated 5.12 xERA; even with the lineup pending, his xwOBA profile against this tier of pitching keeps his floor comfortably high. **Geraldo Perdomo** (62.79) also earns a strong recommendation, utilizing a favorable matchup against Littell to provide necessary stability in the middle of our order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Bryson Stott** (48.56), who narrowly missed the cut behind the more efficient options like **Jonathan Aranda** and **Gleyber Torres**. While **Bryson Stott** benefits from a slow opposing pitcher delivery that would theoretically boost his stolen base potential, his negative platoon split against Eisert ultimately suppressed his projection below our optimal starting threshold. We are also keeping a close eye on the wind conditions impacting **Gleyber Torres** and **Tyler Freeman**; both players receive a meaningful lift from favorable wind projections, though **Tyler Freeman** remains a volatile play given the elite 2.70 xERA of Misiorowski, which forces us to rely heavily on his park factor advantage to maintain his start.\n\nRisks remain throughout the afternoon as we await official word on **Will Smith** and **Gavin Sheets**, both of whom are projected based on assumed lineup spots. While **Jung Hoo Lee** (49.14) is locked into the lineup, his value is predicated on his ability to leverage the slow delivery of Brown, Be, to secure a stolen base, a critical component of our strategy given our emphasis on speed. We continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains sidelined on the IL, leaving us reliant on **Will Smith** to carry the load at catcher without the flexibility of a secondary option.",
